{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-5k.7.1:000001:issue_created:bob-cli-5k.7.1:2fe3cb52fdc380532d4b540b9fb71ef124b59d4853cff6e72c4b126c42b67786","timestamp":"2026-10-07T20:17:59Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-5k.7","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-5k.7.1","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-5k.7.1","title":"Migrate zorg-era reading records into the reference library","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":"bob-cli-5k.7","owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-10-07T20:17:59Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-5k.7","updated_at":"2026-10-07T20:17:59Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"`bob ref migrate-zorg` moves every unindexed zorg-era reading record (424 on 2026-10-07) into legacy reference notes under `ref/zorg/<hub>/`. It runs as a dry-run-first, idempotent vault write: one sync-sandwiched commit that a single `git revert` undoes. Book chapters fold into their book's note. On athena, `bob ref doctor` then reports `coverage: ok`, `bob ref find` / `bob ref list` return the migrated records, the JSON `coverage.scope` caveat no longer claims that zorg history is invisible, and bob-cli-4x is closed.","design":"plan:202610/zorg_ref_migration.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202610/zorg_ref_migration.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
